    "title": "Is the stock market open MLK Day 2026? NYSE, market holidays 2026",
    "text": "NEWSIs the stock market closed on MLK Day 2026? Is Nasdaq, NYSE open? Lori ComstockUSA TODAY NETWORKJan. 12, 2026, 12:25 p.m. ETMartin Luther King Jr. Day is a federal holiday on Monday, Jan. 19, 2026, shutting down federal offices, banks, and post offices, but is the stock market open or closed on MLK Day 2026.MLK Day, or the birthday of Martin Luther King Jr. is celebrated the third Monday in January every year, with this year the holiday on January 19. King, who led the charge for nonviolent activism in the Civil Rights Movement, protesting racial segregation and discrimination in the 1950s, is known for his \"I Have a Dream\" speech on Aug. 28, 1963, during the March on Washington. King's birthday is Jan. 15, and MLK Jr. Day became a holiday in 1983, when it was signed into law by President Ronald Reagan. King was assassinated in 1968.",
